    description: "The National Shrine of Saint Joseph is the primary and historic Catholic church of Mandaue City, located in the heart of the downtown area. It is one of the very few churches in the Philippines dedicated to Saint Joseph as a patron of laborers and families. The current stone structure was built in the early 19th century and features a simple but imposing facade with a large central belfry. Inside, the church is world-famous for its life-sized figures of the Last Supper, which are a focal point of the city's grand Lenten traditions. The interior is spacious and well-ventilated, with beautiful religious murals on the ceiling that have been carefully restored. The church is situated right next to the Mandaue Heritage Plaza and the City Hall, forming the city's traditional town center. Every day, hundreds of worshippers visit the shrine to offer prayers, attend mass, and light candles. It remains the most important and beloved religious landmark in the city of Mandaue. The shrine is a place of deep devotion and peace.",
