    name: "Mandaue-Mactan Bridge (First Bridge)",
    description: "The Mandaue-Mactan Bridge, often called the 'First Bridge' by locals, is a massive and iconic engineering landmark that connects mainland Cebu to Mactan Island. It is a truss bridge that spans the narrow and busy channel, providing a critical link for daily transportation and commerce. The bridge features high steel arches, a long roadway, and wide pedestrian walkways that offer stunning views of the sea and the surrounding cities. Since its completion in 1970, it has been one of the most vital and necessary pieces of infrastructure in the entire region. Every day, thousands of cars, buses, and trucks cross the bridge, supporting the economies of both Mandaue and Lapu-Lapu City. It is particularly beautiful at night when it is lit up with hundreds of bright lights that reflect on the water. The bridge is a symbol of modern Cebu and a favorite subject for local artists, photographers, and visitors. It remains a major landmark for anyone traveling between the international airport and the city center. It is an engineering marvel that changed the region.",
